{
  "schema": 1,
  "kind": "behavioural",
  "machine": "zone",
  "name": "zone_geometry_never_selects_a_synthetic_device",
  "description": "Every device has coordinates so that no feature needs an unmapped code path, but a synthetic device's are arbitrary. A geometric clause that matched them would select the device essentially at random, and random is indistinguishable from broken - a strip that joins 'the bottom of the room' one boot and not the next, with nothing to look at. Refusing to match is the behaviour that turns that into a question the app can answer.",
